'''Hisbanya''' ({{Langx|mxi|إِسْبَانْيَا|Išbânya}}) is a [[Boroughs of Castejón|borough of Castejón]]. In the [[2025 Baliscan census]], it had a population of 456,927 people, making it the least populous of Castejón's twelve boroughs.

Many important administrative institutions of the confederation along with numerous historic parks, monuments and museums are located in Hisbanya. This includes the [[Baliscan Cabildo]], [[Quinta de Viñas]], the [[Metropolitan Council of Castejón]] building and the seats of numerous government agencies, the [[Monumento a la Revolución|Monument to the Revolution]], the [[Museum of Indigenous Peoples]], the [[Northern Institute of the Arts]], the [[Confederal Gallery (Balisca)|Confederal Gallery]], the [[Anhangá Museum]] and the [[Confederal Library (Balisca)|Confederal Library]]. It hosts numerous foreign embassies as well as regional headquarters of many international organizations.

For much of the 20th century the borough maintained stringent {{W|Height restriction laws|height restriction laws}} that prevented the construction of buildings taller than 91 meters (300 feet), resulting in an absence of high-rise buildings that typically characterize the rest of the Metropolis. This changed with the implementation of the [[Casajuan Plan]] in 2014 and the development of [[Nueva Cuenca]] ("new basin"), alongside other rapid [[W:Verticalization|verticalization]].

Hisbanya has adopted ideas of {{W|Ildefons Cerdà}} into it's urban design, and incorporates {{W|urban wild|significant areas of natural vegetation}}. Other notable features include the [[Crystal Palace]], the [[Tidal Basin]] and surrounding [[Parc Sakura]]. Highlights in the annual calendar of cultural events include [[Flowers and Love Festival]], the largest flower festival in the [[Northern Hemisphere|Northern]] and [[Western Hemisphere|Western Hemispheres]], the Fire Festival, [[Kaftopunk]], the [[Immigrant's Festival (Balisca)|Immigrant's Festival]] and [[Festival de la Humanitá]]. Major main sporting venues include [[Simpliciano Stadium]] and the [[Montjuïc Oval]].

